      "widgets_values": [
        "TARGET-MATCHED UNIT ICON\n\nThe 128x128 output is the canonical Godot asset. The 512x512 file is only a 4x nearest-neighbor preview.\n\nFaction schemes:\n- target: supplied reference colors\n- germany: exact black, purple-grey, field-grey colors from pixel1\n- allies: exact olive, green, teal colors from pixel1\n\nProfile safe boxes:\n- infantry: compact 66x52\n- vehicle: wide 80x46\n- artillery: long 90x38\n\nUse AUTO for normal batches, or force a profile when a source is classified incorrectly.\n\nsubject_threshold controls which dark pixels belong to the source silhouette. Raise it for pale grey vectors; lower it if an old circular frame is being retained.\n\nThe ellipse, faction palette, transparency, framing, and output sizes are deterministic."
      ],
      "color": "#243",
      "bgcolor": "#465"
    },
